\section*{B. 4 Force convergence plots on the filtered set}

The final OC25 dataset ultimately filtered samples with a total drift \(<1 \mathrm{eV} / \AA\) to ensure the dataset is broadly useful beyond just MLIP training. Figure 7 corresponds to a model trained on the released OC25 dataset (converged with EDIFF \(=10^{-4} \mathrm{eV}\), but with all images with total drift \(>1 \mathrm{eV} / \AA\) removed) and evaluated on the validation set with the same drift filtering. The small gap between force errors at EDIFF \(=10^{-4} \mathrm{eV}\) ) and (EDIFF \(=10^{-6} \mathrm{eV}\) ) suggests that the total drift filter does a reasonable job at removing problematic samples in the training set.

